<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Kunihar State</h1><p class="st-meta">1154 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Kunihar</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">One of the smallest of the Simla Hill States, a Rajput chiefship near Shimla restored under British protection after the Gurkha wars.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Tradition holds that the ruling family came from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akhnoor">Akhnoor</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jammu">Jammu</a> and founded the state around 1154.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Kunihar consisted of a few villages in the hills west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shimla">Shimla</a>, ruled by a Thakur or Rana. Like its neighbours it was occupied by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gurkhas">Gurkhas</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-nepal">Kingdom of Nepal</a> in the early 19th century; little else is recorded of its history.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The British restored the ruler by sanad in 1815. Kunihar merged into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/himachal-pradesh">Himachal Pradesh</a> in April 1948 and is now in Solan district.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kunihar-state.jpg" alt="Kunihar State" width="320" height="240"><figcaption>Image: Bhanu Sharma Solan · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kunihar_valley_Solan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1154 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kunihar</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Western Pahari</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kunihar</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1551&amp;focus=kunihar-state" aria-label="Kunihar State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6670 1045 640 512" role="img" aria